  "id": "terukkuttu_kattaikkuttu",
  "name": "Terukkuttu / Kattaikkuttu (Tamil Mahabharata street theatre)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Terukkuttu ('street theatre'), called Kattaikkuttu by its performers, is the all-night village theatre of northern Tamil Nadu that enacts episodes of the Mahabharata, above all during Draupadi temple festivals. Actors sing their own verses, which a chorus standing behind them repeats, over an ensemble of harmonium, mukhavina (a small double-reed pipe), mridangam and cymbals. The Kattaikkuttu Sangam, based near Kanchipuram, trains young performers, and Richard Frasca's study documented its performances.",
  "recipe": "classic modern terukkuttu / kattaikkuttu, ballad Poetry, indian bard branch. jackwood barrel canonical Tamil mridangam, song accompaniment harmonium indian, mukhavina, small manjira. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
